send_cmd: limit the reply length to the reply buffer

send_cmd_rx takes the number of reply bytes from the client and hands it to
read_string() unchecked: read_string() first clears that many bytes of the
512 byte reply buffer and then fills them, so a large length overwrites the
stack and a negative one, taken as a size, runs off it.

Not reached with the Dummy rig, which answers without a port.

diff --git a/tests/rigctl_parse.c b/tests/rigctl_parse.c
--- a/tests/rigctl_parse.c
+++ b/tests/rigctl_parse.c
@@ -5392,6 +5392,12 @@ declare_proto_rig(send_cmd)
             eom_buf[0] = 0;
         }
 
+        /* [RADE] The length is the client's; read_string() clears and fills
+         * as many bytes of buf as it is told. */
+        if (rxbytes < 0) { rxbytes = 0; }
+
+        if (rxbytes > BUFSZ) { rxbytes = BUFSZ; }
+
         if (simulate)
         {
             if (retval == 0)
